<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Man dies at MIM mine, no output halt.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Man dies at MIM mine, no output halt.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>A man was crushed to death on Sunday while working underground at the Mount Isa base metals and silver mine in north-central Queensland state, a spokeswoman for the mine's owner, MIM Holdings Ltd, said on Monday.</p>
<p>Mine output was not affected by the accident, she said.</p>
<p>It is the second time a miner has been killed in a mine in Australia in five days.</p>
<p>Last Wednesday, a man died in a rockfall at WMC Ltd's Rocky's Reward nickel mine in Western Australia.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
